    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98-a4">

                <pb facs="0227" n="187" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg187"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure No. 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Nesbet to Mr.
                        Kirkpatrick.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colonial Secretary’s Office</hi>. <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Nassau,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 31, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>. I am directed by the governor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your letter of this date, and, in reply, to express
                    his excellency’s regret that he is restricted from granting the leave requested
                    on behalf of the United States. ship-of-war Honduras to anchor in this harbor to
                    transact some business with this consulate in regard to payment of salvage to
                    the wreckers of the United States ship San Jacinto, lately wrecked, except “in
                    cases of grave emergency, and of real necessity and distress;” and his
                    excellency requests that you will lose no time in conveying this reply to the
                    commander of the Honduras.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. R. NESBET, <hi rendition="#italic">Colonial
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas Kirkpatrick</hi>. Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul, Nassau, N. P.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
